"""Separate additive closing transports; never rewrite a previously published transport."""
import pathlib,json,hashlib
root=pathlib.Path.cwd();out=pathlib.Path(__file__).parent;prefix='docs/evidence/audit-remediation-20260927/r01-forward/';evidence=root/prefix;old=json.loads((evidence/'task-12-receipts/fix1-translation.json').read_bytes());seen={e['originalPath']for e in old['entries']};entries=[]
for p in sorted(out.rglob('*')):
 if not p.is_file():continue
 path=p.relative_to(root).as_posix()
 if path in seen:continue
 raw=p.read_bytes();sha=hashlib.sha256(raw).hexdigest();archive=evidence/'task-12-receipts/blobs'/(sha+'.source')
 if archive.exists():assert archive.read_bytes()==raw
 else:archive.write_bytes(raw)
 entries.append({'originalPath':path,'archivePath':archive.relative_to(root).as_posix(),'rawSha256':sha,'canonicalSha256':hashlib.sha256(raw.replace(b'\r\n',b'\n')).hexdigest(),'rawGitBlob':hashlib.sha1(b'blob '+str(len(raw)).encode()+b'\0'+raw).hexdigest(),'rawBytes':len(raw),'evidenceKind':'task12-i1-new-closing-metadata-transport'})
value={'receiptVersion':1,'mode':'task12-i1-additive-closing-transport','error':None,'entries':entries,'priorFix1TransportSha256':hashlib.sha256((evidence/'task-12-receipts/fix1-translation.json').read_bytes()).hexdigest(),'closingGitVerified':False,'sameReviewerApproved':False,'freshFiveCiVerified':False,'productionApplied':False,'qualification':'Post-publication source/preservation/closing records are additive. Transport is not readiness acceptance.'};(evidence/'task-12-receipts/fix1-closing-translation.json').write_bytes((json.dumps(value,indent=2)+'\n').encode())
allEntries={e['originalPath']:e for e in old['entries']+entries}
def pin(name):return allEntries[(out/name).relative_to(root).as_posix()]
path=evidence/'task-12-fix1-source-binding.json';binding=json.loads(path.read_bytes());binding['metadataPreservationReceipt']=pin('close-receipt.json');binding['metadataPreservationDriver']=pin('close.py');binding['metadataPreservationDriverPrearchive']=pin('close-executed.source');binding['completeExecutableAppendix']={name:pin(name)for name in ['binder-correct.py','tests-correct.py','run-correct.py','prepare.py','fixtures-correct.py','fixture-correct.py','correct-generator-fix.py','prepare-correction.py','package.py','run-package.py','close.py','tail-package.py','tail-run.py']};binding['historicalFailureExecutableAppendix']={name:pin(name)for name in ['binder.py','tests.py','run.py','fixtures.py','correct.py']};binding['preservationActualCounts']={'oldOriginal':41773,'oldClosing':340,'oldImmutable230RawGitArchivePaths':2018,'newFix1Originals':329,'newClosingOriginals':len(entries)};binding['loaderClosure']='GREEN runs tests-correct.py, which imports binder-correct.py and loads every prearchived fixtures/*.json definition. Actual acceptance runs binder-correct.py; only Python standard-library modules are imported. Synthetic cases were built by fixtures-correct.py through fixture-correct.py, importing the historical weak RED binder.py only for literal flag constants. No actual receipts are imported by portable tests. Preparation and metadata transport/closing sources are individually archived.';path.write_bytes((json.dumps(binding,indent=2)+'\n').encode());print(json.dumps({'additionalClosingLocators':len(entries),'oldAndFirstFix1TransportsUnchanged':True}))
